== Debate format ==
The second debate was structured as a three-hour program divided into six segments:
# The ACTA Downgrade and Economic Recovery
# The Satori Blackout and Digital Infrastructure
# Rail Safety and the Two-Man Mandate
# Social Welfare and the Cost of Living
# Foreign Policy and Regional Security
# Closing Statements

Each segment began with an opening statement from a minor party leader, followed by a moderator question directed at a major party candidate, and concluding with open discussion among all seven participants. The format was deliberately expanded from the first debate to accommodate the full field of party leaders.

The debate was moderated by '''Aiko Hasegawa''' of Asahi Okaiken, the only senior female political moderator in Sanese broadcast journalism. At 52, Hasegawa brought three decades of experience and a reputation for incisive, non-partisan questioning. Her selection was seen as an attempt to restore credibility to the debate format after the controversial first debate.

